# uniti.sty - UNITI presentation rules (built-in)
#
# Ordinary .sty records whose \Marker is a CSS-like selector instead of a
# marker name. They take the normal STY fields (FontSize, Bold, Italic,
# Superscript, SpaceBefore, LeftMargin, FirstLineIndent, ...) and apply on
# top of the styled marker's own style in UNITI's Standard and Preview views.
#
#   \Marker p+q1        a \q1 paragraph straight after a \p paragraph
#   \Marker f::caller   the caller of a footnote
#
# Several selectors can share one record, separated by commas. A numberless
# marker and its level-1 form match each other (q = q1, s = s1). A flag such
# as \Bold is turned off again with "\Bold -".
#
# A record with an ordinary marker name (\Marker nd) changes that
# marker's own style, like any other stylesheet layer.
#
# Project rules go in a file named uniti.sty next to the book files. It
# layers on top of every other stylesheet, and Paratext and PTXprint never
# read it.

\Marker f::caller, fe::caller, ef::caller
\Name Note caller - Footnote
\Superscript
\Bold

\Marker x::caller, ex::caller
\Name Note caller - Cross Reference
\Superscript
\Italic

\Marker p+q1, p+q2, p+q3, q1+p, q2+p, q3+p
\Name Blank line between prose and poetry
\SpaceBefore 12

\Marker nd
\Name nd - Name of Deity, shown in small capitals
\SmallCaps
\Underline -

\Marker cat
\Endmarker cat*
\Name cat...cat* - Category of a note or sidebar, shown in brackets in Preview
\StyleType Character
\TextProperties publishable
\Italic
